  "claims": [
    "Channel filling preferably less than 10%.",
    "The measured saturation profile was not influenced by different lateral lengths of the LHAR channel (100 µm to 5 mm).",
    "With increasing TMA dose, the growth transformed from TMA-dose-limited to water-dose-limited.",
    "Changes in the saturation profile were observed with increasing purge times.",
    "Lumped sticking coefficients calculated from the slope of the saturation profile agreed with previously reported values.",
    "The larger the channel height, the deeper the film penetrated.",
    "For a channel height of 100 nm, the adsorption front began with no preceding constant thickness region.",
    "Film penetration, measured as PD 50%, appeared to decrease as the number of cycles increased.",
    "The penetration depth increased with increasing TMA pulse time, showing a dependency on the precursor dose.",
    "For a TMA pulse time of 0.4 s, the adsorption front was notably broadened compared to pulse times of 0.1 and 0.2 s, while GPC remained similar.",
    "The TMA dose no longer limited the film growth, and the saturation profile was defined by the water dose.",
    "The GPC slightly decreased when the purge time increased from 1 to 10 s, while PD 50% slightly increased.",
    "TMA-limited and water-limited growth has different characteristic shape of the saturation profile at 300 °C.",
    "During longer purge, reversibly adsorbed water molecules could have desorbed, causing a decrease in the concentration of surface OH groups.",
    "The amount of TMA adsorbed decreased as the amount of TMA adsorbed depends on the concentration of surface OH groups.",
    "GPC decreased as purge time increased (from 1 s to 4 s).",
    "A higher GPC of the TMA-water ALD process was reported for higher water partial pressure.",
    "Reversible reaction of water was assumed.",
    "A long purge time can alter GPC due to dehydration on the surface.",
    "The decrease in binding capacity of the surface towards TMA enabled the reactant molecules to penetrate deeper into the channel before reacting, resulting in an increased penetration depth.",
    "Increased penetration depth (in PillarHall-1) with decreased GPC has been observed in earlier works by Mattinen et al. for iridium ALD and by Puurunen and Gao for Al2O3 ALD at different temperatures."
  ]
}